{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And it was when they brought them outside.</b> It should have said 'when they brought them outside'; rather, Scripture teaches with 'them' — specifically them they brought out, and not their property. This teaches that Lot was running after his property to bring it out, and they did not let him — like 'and your carcasses, you.' Another interpretation: and it was when the angels brought out <b>them</b> — et Lot and et his household." "<b>Do not look behind you.</b> Because of the distress of your sons-in-law who are in the city — and run quickly on your way, and do not stop to look here and there, for the cloud is rising and in it is fire and sulfur, and it is spreading over the entire land." "<b>Do not look.</b> He warned him and all who are his, and therefore his wife was stricken. And a parallel to this we find in the portion of Genesis: 'and from the tree of knowledge of good and evil you shall not eat from it' — it implies that neither you nor all who are yours shall eat, and therefore Eve was stricken. 'Do not look' — the bet has a hireq dot."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:04:55.357010621Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}